# Line endings are part of this project's ABI.
#
# `sqlx::migrate!` hashes the RAW BYTES of every file in src-tauri/migrations at
# compile time and writes that hash into the `_sqlx_migrations` table the first
# time a migration runs. Git's `core.autocrlf` (set to `true` system-wide by the
# Git for Windows installer) means two machines can check the same commit out
# with different line endings, so their binaries embed different hashes for
# byte-identical SQL. Each build then refuses to open a database created by the
# other:
#
#     Migrate(VersionMismatch(1))  ->  panic during setup(), window flashes and closes
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF everywhere makes every build machine — laptop,
# desktop, CI — produce identical bytes and therefore identical checksums.
# Rust, Node, and MSVC all handle LF sources fine on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files that are actually checksummed.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Files git must never rewrite.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.rten binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.msi  binary
